Marble Head wrote in message <395A16A1.4FD5DDC8@nospam.guacamole.com>...
>Can somebody tell me how to start a keyboard scrollback buffer, so the
>Up and Down keys retrieve previous commands?
>
>If you don't know what I'm talking about, in DOS and Windows the command
>is doskey.
>
Of the shells installed as standard on Tru64, under ksh, dtksh and sh(1p)
you can use the command:

set -o emacs

Under sh(1b) and csh you are out of luck.
If you are willing to install other shells then bash, tcsh and zsh can
all also provide this functionality.

Hope this helps
Adam






