At "Managed Pages Break Down" you can see something called ubc pages.
This is the unified buffer cache. This will grow if you have a system
with high activity and free memory, thus decreasing the free memory. If
some programs need more memory it'll be given to them causing a decrease
in the ubc size.
So you can to some degree consider a large part of ubc allocated memory
to be free for user space code.

A big allocater is the filesystem cache :

