This was on the Tru64 FAQ page but under "miscellaneous" section 
not sections alpha" and "software" (where I had already looked(!)).
(Sorry for asking a question which was already in the FAQ)

FYI the solution is 

M17. Why does dxaccounts tells me that the password and
      group files are locked

If a dxaccounts process exits ungracefully (e.g. if a kill -9
is used) then it sometimes leaves a file in /etc called .AM_is_running.
Deleting this file will solve the problem. 

                                    [Ian Lloyd]

> (2) How does one add daemons so that they are started automatically 
> when the system boots up. i.e. in linux it is by putting the commands 
> in e.g. /etc/rc.d/rc.3/Snncommand.  What is the Digital Unix equivalent?

The relevant directory is e.g. /sbin/rc3.d.

Mike




