In your steps 2, 3, 4, 5, you will need to use the non-rewind device
each time
(that is /dev/nrmt0h). Otherwise, command 4 (for example) will move the
tape ahead by 1 saveset,
but then rewind the tape when finishing.

Apart from that, it should work.
It is fairly easy to elaborate on this; for example, dd the list of file
systems and a date
stamp as the first file on the tape, then build a little restore script
which will read
the label, and given a file system name, figure out how much fsf'ing to
do, so you can selectively
restore by specifying names etc. etc. But if you are going to that much
trouble, maybe you should
consider Amanda.

Hope this helps.

