In article <20000613114848.11558.00005973@ng-ch1.aol.com>,
Tom Sevy <tsevy@aol.comnospam> wrote:
> We are going to be bringing Tru64 in house.  What is the closest relative in
> the *nix world to start getting a feel for Tru64 that will run on either a 433a
> (not au) or on the x86 platform?

One of the *BSD derivatives would probably be closest, though there are
significant differences.

> Or what is the cheapest used system generally available that will run Tru64?

You can often find old alphastations on various Internet auction sites.  I
picked up a barebones *new* AlphaStation 200 4/233 for about $300, but to
add the disk, CDROM, 128 MB+ of RAM, and a decent video card the total probably
came to over $1,000.  You might be better off buying a new 433/au, which I've
seen for $1,400 from some places with everything you need (low on RAM though).
That price may be lower by now, though 433s are probably getting to be hard
to find.

Tim
