In article <8sM%4.13003$bH5.636951@nntp1.onemain.com>,
Djones <dalejava@freeshell.org> wrote:
> I noticed I'm getting errors in my daemaon.log file from syslog.dated.
> 
> inetd[6450]: netbios-ns/udp: bind: Address already in use
> inetd[6450]: bootps/udp: bind: Address already in use

When it says `bind', it's not talking about named, it's talking about bind(2),
so restarting named won't do any good.

The message is telling you that inetd can't start services on those two ports
because something has already bound (past tense of bind) to that port.  This
most likely means that you're trying to run things on those ports both via
"standalone" daemons and via inetd (the standalones are starting first, since
inetd is the one that's complaining).

You need to figure out why you have two instances of those two services
starting, and eliminate one instance (either the standalone or the inetd
service, it's up to you).

Tim
