I should also mention that the latest Compaq C compiler
in the Developer's Toolkit Supplement adds some useful
diagnostics that will help you port the code.

The compiler is available for download at:

  http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/dtk/

The compiler can be installed on Tru64 UNIX Version 4.0D,
4.0F, 4.0G, 5.0, and 5.0A. It does not require an
additional license, if you already have an active
software development (OSF_DEV) license.

You'll want the latest Field Test kit (available 6/9/00)
In the man page, you can read about how to turn on (or
off) some of the additional diagnostics.

For example, you could add "-msg_enable level[n]" or
"-msg_enable 64bit". You can use -msg_disable to quiet
any of the warnings that are not of interest. If you
don't want to change Makefiles, I suggest you use the
DEC_CC environment variable (or comp.config file).
See man cc(1) for details.

Hope it helps.

-Jeff



