> 
>   If anybody can suggest ways of making my LaserJet shine to its full
> potential it would be appreciated.

Hi,

there is an unsupported print filter called ppdof that works with ppd
files. Those can be obtained from Adobe's web site for most PS printers.
If you find one for your LaserJet then you are able to use all the
features that appear in the ppd file via -O switches. Tru64 4.0x
supports one of them at a time, 5.0x supports multiple -O switches.
I haven't tested all possible features of our LaserJet 4M+ setup but at
least choosing the paper source works now. That was the most important
thing for us.
If you are interested in that ppdof filter kit, send me an e-mail, and
I'll send it to you.

Regards,
Ralf Eichmann



