>I don't know how to mount automaticaly disk partition at boot time.

look at /etc/fstab

Also "man fstab" for an explination of all the fields in the /etc/fstab
file.  If memory mounted file systems are also desirable, then see "man
mfs" as well as "man fstab"

/dev/rz0a      swap1   ufs   sw 0 2
/dev/rz16b     swap2   ufs   sw 0 2
/dev/rz17b     swap2   ufs   sw 0 2

/dev/rz16a     /tmp    ufs   rw 1 2

domain1#fset1  /fset1  advfs rw,userquota,groupquota 1 2

/freeware@some.ones.system.com  /freeware  nfs ro,bg 0 0
some.node.com:/stuff            /stuff     nfs ro,bg 0 0

-s65536                         /memory_mounted_filesys mfs rw 0 0

Note, in V5.0 and newer, the specification of the swap device moves to
the /etc/sysconfigtab file.



