This a bug which was found and should be fixed in the available patch
kits <http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/support.html>

If you need to address this before installing a patch, the short term
work-around is to run the quotacheck utility to fix-up the quota
information (AdvFS always maintains quota, it is just not enforced
unless enabled by the customer).

You may need to add userquota,groupquota options to your /etc/fstab
file:

  root_domain#root  /  advfs  rw,userquota,groupquota  0 1

Again, this does not actually change the way AdvFS works, but it allows
the quotacheck utility to work on the fileset.

                                        Bob Harris



