> branded "Kingston" but is 21140 based.....

The 2114x chipsets are known to cause problems when autonegotiating
speed with hubs/switches.
Symptoms are usually very bad transmission speed (easy to see by FTP'ing
a large file), or no connection at all, allthough the link usually is
OK.

The magic environment variable is ewa0_mode for tu0, ewb0_mode for tu1
and so on.
Do a show ew* to see what's present.

It can be set to something like Fast, FastFD, Twisted-Pair, Auto. I
might've missed one or mispelled one, but as far as I remember you can
see the possible choices by doing a help ewa0_mode or setting it to
something invalid like "set ewa0_mode help".


