I'm no expert so I could be wrong, but I think the answer is no.  Support
for a particular video card in Tru64 comes in two parts.  Part one is
"console support", which is the "bare bones" support for the video card
itself.  Part two is an X DDX, which is the component that makes the card
work under X.  Part two requires part one.

Again, I could be horribly mistaken.  You may wish to read through the
online guide for device driver writers, which should hopefully clear up
any errors in what I've said:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/dev_doc/DOCUMENTATION/HTML/Digital_UNIX_Bookshelf.html
