:> Unfortunately, the card in the machine turns out to be 
:> branded "Kingston" but is 21140 based.....

: Are you sure this card will work with Tru64?

Mmmm. Herein lies the problem.
SRM sees a tulip and tells Tru64 that you have an ethernet interface.
Tru64 queries the SROM on the card to check what media type is appropriate.
Seeing a tulip and no SROM, the tulip driver chucks a hissy fit and won't let
you force the media type, or send any traffic across the interface, as it
doesn't know what's plugged in.
This is why I paid AU$50 to get myself a 2ndhand DE500 - I've already played
these games with my PC164.

Apparently the Intel Etherexpress pro100 or similar will work with a BETA
driver if you can get it... but I'd trawl Ebay for a DE500/450/435.

